@startuml component_activation

title Component Activation

box "Main loop thread" #F0F4FA
participant "ProcessGroupManager" as PGM
participant "Graph" as Graph
participant "Transition" as Transition
end box

queue "Worker Queue" as WorkerQueue
queue "Component Event Queue" as EventQueue

box "Worker thread" #FAF6F0
participant "IComponentController" as Monitor
participant "IComponent" as Component
end box

participant "SafeProcessMap" as Map
participant "Alive Supervision" as Supervision
participant "Operating System" as OS

note over Graph: graph is in state kInTransition

' --- dispatch ----------------------------------------------------------------
activate Graph
Graph -> Transition ++: get components ready to be started
Transition --> Graph --: component is ready to be started
Graph -> WorkerQueue: activation of the component
note over Graph
  The graph only counts the component as in flight.
  The main loop does not wait for it and returns to
  consuming events.
end note
deactivate Graph

' --- execution ---------------------------------------------------------------
WorkerQueue -> Monitor ++: activation is taken by a free worker
Monitor -> Component ++: activate

loop one iteration per configured startup attempt
    Component -> OS ++: start the process

    alt #Pink the process cannot be started
        OS --> Component --: start failed
        note right of Component
          Final: a launch failure is not retried.
          The component is left in its failed state.
        end note

    else #White the process was started
        OS --> Component --: process started
        Component -> Map ++: register the started process PID
        note right of Component
          The registration is what lets the OsHandler thread
          route a later termination of this process back to
          this component - see Component Deactivation.
        end note

        alt #Pink the process cannot be registered
            Map --> Component --: no capacity left
            Component -> OS: stop the process that was started
            note right of Component
              Final: a registration failure is not retried.
            end note

        else #FFF8E8 the process has already exited
            Map --> Component --: the process has already exited
            note right of Component
              The OsHandler thread recorded the exit before this
              registration arrived; the map resolves the race in
              either order. A component that reports its readiness
              counts this as a failed attempt, one that does not is
              judged by its exit code.
            end note

        else #FFF8E8 the ready condition is not reached in time
            Map --> Component --: process registered
            Component -> Component: wait for the ready condition\nuntil the ready timeout expires
            Component -> OS ++: stop the process that was started
            OS --> Component --: process stopped
            note right of Component
              A timed out attempt is retried while attempts
              are left.The last attempt fails the activation.
              A transition cancelled between two attempts also
              ends the activation here - see Transition
              Cancellation / Preemption.
            end note

        else #F2FAF2 the ready condition is satisfied
            Map --> Component --: process registered
            opt ready condition is not "process started"
                Component -> Component: wait for the ready condition\n(Running report, configured file or own termination)
                note right of Component
                  A component whose ready condition is its own
                  termination waits for the exit of its process.
                  That exit is observed on the OsHandler thread,
                  which releases the waiting worker - see Process
                  Termination.
                end note
            end
            opt component is supervised
                Component -> Supervision ++: start supervising the process
                Supervision --> Component --: supervision active
            end
        end
    end
end

' --- result ------------------------------------------------------------------
alt the ready condition was satisfied
    Component --> Monitor: ready condition satisfied
    Monitor -> EventQueue: component activated successfully
else no attempt succeeded
    Component --> Monitor: activation failed\n(no attempt reached the ready condition)
    Monitor -> EventQueue: component failed to activate
end
deactivate Component
deactivate Monitor

' --- completion --------------------------------------------------------------
EventQueue -> PGM ++: component event
PGM -> Graph ++: apply the component event

alt the event reports a successful activation
    Graph -> Transition ++: component has finished
    Transition --> Graph --: next components ready to be started
    note over Graph
      Once the transition reports that nothing is left,
      the graph moves to kSuccess.
    end note

else the event reports a failed activation
    Graph -> Graph: leave the transition
    note over Graph
      The graph moves to kAborting. The components still in
      flight finish their current step and report back.
      Components that are already running stay running.
    end note
end

deactivate Graph
deactivate PGM

legend bottom
  The two queues are the only interaction between the threads: the graph never
  touches a component directly and a worker never touches the graph. All graph
  and transition state stays confined to the main loop thread.

  Several components may be in flight at the same time; a single one is shown
  here for clarity.
end legend

@enduml
